; The system's random generator, and nothing else from this library.
;
; ⭐ ProcessPrng RATHER THAN BCryptGenRandom, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS A HANDLE.
; The documented CNG entry point takes an algorithm handle, which this backend
; would have to open on every call or cache — and caching one means having an
; initialisation order. `ProcessPrng` is the same generator without the handle;
; it has been present since Windows 10 and is what Chromium and Rust's standard
; library moved to for these reasons.
;
; Generated into an import library by build.mcpp; see port/README.md.
LIBRARY bcryptprimitives.dll
EXPORTS
ProcessPrng
